  "projects": {
    "agent1-periodic-cycle-adapter": {
      "status": "PASS",
      "scope": "Conditional realization of repeated copies of one supplied positive-length exact period-four full quotient cycle from original-valid initial data. Literal natural copy guards retain a fixed initial exponent and one ordinary seed for all times. Explicit safePeriodic=true at every finite cycle state supplies all-time nonpalindromicity of the successor seed through existing numeric safety. This formalizes the original METHOD section4 positive-cycle criterion. No qualifying cycle is constructed; no unconditional decimal existence, 196 result, arbitrary graph-cycle realization, safety-preservation theorem, or finite-witness quantifier swap is asserted.",
